## Why This Is Asked

Assesses handling of articulated, hinge-based objects in clutter, real-time constraints, and on-device adaptation with few shots.

## Key Concepts

- Articulated 6-DoF pose estimation for hinged objects
- Hinge-state (open/closed) inference
- Synthetic+real data with domain adaptation
- Few-shot on-device fine-tuning
- Real-time edge deployment considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pose error metric example (illustrative)
function poseError(est, gt) {
  // est/gt: {R: rotation matrix, t: translation vector}
  const rotError = rotationDistance(est.R, gt.R);
  const transError = vectorDistance(est.t, gt.t);
  return { rotError, transError };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you mitigate pose ambiguity from symmetric trays?
- How would you extend to add new hinge geometries online without retraining a large model?

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses end-to-end CV system design on monocular input, 3D reconstruction, semantic/kinematic outputs, and on-device adaptation, under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth/3D reconstruction
- Voxel-based 3D representation and BEV outputs
- Multi-task objectives: occupancy, semantics, motion tracking
- Self-supervision with ego-motion and photometric consistency
- Lightweight 3-shot on-device adaptation via adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch
async function runPipeline(frame) {
  const latent = encode(frame)
  const voxels = decodeToVoxels(latent)
  return { occupancy: voxelToOccupancy(voxels), beings: trackPedestrians(latent) }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate 3D occupancy accuracy vs. GT? 
- How would you extend to multi-camera fusion or hinge on motion blur?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world constraints: on-device adaptation, occlusion robustness, and AR-friendly latency for indoor property inspections. Probes data strategy and robust evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose from RGB
- On-device 5-shot adaptation
- Synthetic + real data strategy
- Occlusion-robust tracking
- Edge GPU latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: simple adaptation step
function adapt(batch) {
  for (const [x, y] of batch) {
    const pred = model.predict(x);
    const loss = poseLoss(pred, y);
    optimizer.step(loss);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you compare on-device adaptation strategies under varying illumination?
- What metrics best detect drift in furniture appearance over time?
